{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024297-need-an-explaination-please-small-words","id":1024297,"title":"Need an explaination please (small words)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-30T07:14:03-08:00","id":1024297,"title":"Need an explaination please (small words)","content":"OK, I'm an old school Ascension player who is finally reading Awakening. I am having a little trouble understanding the whole relationship between Orders, Paths, Legacies. I get that a Path is the way your soul is attuned to magic, and the Orders are the political organizations of Awakened. However, I'm not really sure where Legacies fit into the whole thing. Reading about them on the wiki, they certainly feel more like the Traditions, but if they are their own organizations how do they fit in with Orders? In the local, national, international power structures are you Order first, Legacy second? Is it more like, say, being a Democrat in the American Congress (Order) and also a member of, say, the Congressional Black Caucus (Legacy)? Also, Attainments? How do those work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:23:40-08:00","id":1024302,"title":"","content":"The relation between order and legacy is like the relation between being a physicist and being a condensed matter physicist, or a biologist and a marine ethologist. It's a group of people all interested in doing the same, highly specialized thing, which in turn shapes their souls. They're usually too small in number to be a real 'organization' or have political power as a group, but of course someone with political clout can always set himself up as a head of a consilium and then seed it with his legacy disciples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:46:31-08:00","id":1024316,"title":"","content":"A Legacy is what allows the mage to specialize in her field of magic, on top of the broad foundation provided by her Path. At the same time, it also gives you a smaller social clique within an order, sometimes even between orders. In other words, Legacies are both personal and social.<br /> <br /> Whether a mage is more loyal to his order or Legacy depends on individuals. It's sorta like a job and a hobby club. Some people may be defined more by their career, with their hobby a refreshing turn every now and then. Some people may be defined more by their personal pursuits, with their job a means to acquire basic living.<br /> <br /> Attainments are powers a mage acquires by shaping her soul. Or, more correctly, the spiritual vessel that holds her soul. It is both a badge of honor recording your progress on enlightenment as the Legacy taught you, and a nifty trick you get as part of joining a prestige club that is the Legacy. They are valuable because, despite being magical, they are not Supernal and thus are not subject to Paradox, Dissonance, and Quiescence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:37:20-08:00","id":1024357,"title":"","content":"Good to point is that in 2E, Legacy members are Sympathetically linked to one another. That means that you are much more easier to find themselves in local region - but it also means that if Left Hand mages kidnap one of your Legacy members, it can be <i>very</i> dangerous to whole Legacy.<br /> <br /> Also, both Orders and Legacies are said to have Temenos realms where non-physical meetings can commerce. This way of lore and information exchange even <i>created</i> Orders and Legacies in first place, where in <i>Sundered World</i> <b>Dark Era </b>( circa 5500 BCE ) first mages started to meet in Astral and made local proto-cabals and ground works for Legacies. Technically, Legacies predates Orders as in <i>To the Strongest </i><b>Dark Era</b> ( circa 300 BCE, just after Alexander Empire ) there are numerous Legacies and many smaller ( Darshana ) cults, but Diamond Orders as centralized entities are only song of next 100 years. More on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">history and timeline of setting in this topic</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-30-2016, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:34:25-08:00","id":1024423,"title":"","content":"Comparing to Ascension, I would say that Legacies are like a development on Paradigm. An Order or Path talks a lot about your magic, but in quite general terms. The Path talks about your magic, but mostly on how it came to be and what kind of effect you'll be drawn to (it's isn't unlike the Avatar). The Order is an organization with some broad view about the best route to achieve knowledge, and political bodies (similar to the Council of Nine Traditions itself, more than to the Traditions individually, or to a very broad view of a Tradition, but without any particulars).<br /> <br /> Mostly, exploring further your order will be about politics, hierarchy and resources.<br /> <br /> What will customize your view on magic itself and its role on your life, this is Legacy. In Ascension terms, it isn't neither Avatar nor Tradition/Convention, but the Paradigm itself. With a little sense of community thrown in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:54:54-08:00","id":1024431,"title":"","content":"Paths are like loose threads that when pulled unravel some particular aspect of the The Lie.<br /> <br /> Orders are organizations of like minded Mages who share a common idea of what Magic means to them.<br /> <br /> Legacies are smaller groups, more like traditions that survive by being passed from Master to Apprentice. They are based on some very especific and usually radical idea, to which members dedicate their study.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:51:08-08:00","id":1024509,"title":"","content":"The book explains that Paths are how you connect to Magic, they colour your perception of it, as the lens through which you see the world.<br /> The Orders provide guidelines as to how you should use your Magic, and provide a support network and skills so that you can do so.<br /> Legacies however are a narrow view on the application of Magic that you define yourself by.<br /> <br /> So a Moros Mage sees the world as constant change, death is not the end and progress is inevitable.<br /> He might join the Mysterium because he sees the pursuit of mystical knowledge as being a worthy ends in and of itself.<br /> However he might join the legacy of the Stone Scribes, because he wishes to catalogue the lives of the dead by inscribing their true names on stone tablets, drawing upon their power and knowledge in his pursuit of mystical knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}